  "description": "Install a 41.4kWp roof-mounted solar photovoltaic (PV) system comprising 92 panels on the central (nave) roof slope of St Barnabas Church (Grade II listed, within a conservation area), using low-profile mounting rails/fixings, together with associated cabling, inverter and electrical isolation equipment routed discretely to the existing plant room. Provision is included for a 13.49kWh battery energy storage system located within the plant room (subject to final fire safety/insurer requirements). No change of use and no demolition.\n\nA faculty application has also been submitted to the Diocese of Southwark DAC under the Church of England Faculty Jurisdiction.",
